<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH EXPORT BANK SAYS SEES EUROBOND BY END-MAY.</title>
<headline>CZECH EXPORT BANK SAYS SEES EUROBOND BY END-MAY.</headline>
<dateline>BRNO, Czech Republic 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Export Bank (CEB) on Wednesday said it expects to issue a $200-300 million, five-year Eurobond by the end of May, lead-managed by investment bank J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p>CEB Chief Secretary Ondrej Kvacek told Reuters conditions for loan, which will be used to help finance the bank's activities in extending export loans, are still being negotiated.</p>
</text>
